# 3. CRITICAL SOURCE-DISCIPLINE RULE

You MUST distinguish four things throughout the work:

### A. SOURCE CLAIM

What a document explicitly says.

### B. MATHEMATICAL FACT

What can actually be established mathematically from definitions, assumptions and derivations.

### C. VERIFIER INFERENCE

A conclusion you derive while analysing the corpus.

### D. OPEN / UNVERIFIED

Something that cannot currently be established.

Never silently transform A into B.

Never transform C into A.

Never transform "not disproven" into "proven".

Never transform "tested conceptually" into "empirically verified".

Never transform "architecturally useful" into "mathematically true".

