Distinguish:

### Definition gap

A required concept has no precise definition.

### Type gap

An object has no valid type/domain/codomain.

### Assumption gap

A derivation requires an unstated assumption.

### Proof gap

A conclusion is asserted without proof.

### Consistency gap

Two accepted statements contradict each other.

### Completeness gap

The theory lacks a required component.

### Identifiability gap

The claimed quantity cannot be established from available observations.

### Measurement gap

A metric lacks a valid measurement model.

### Statistical gap

A probability/statistical claim lacks required assumptions.

### Computational gap

A formally defined operation may not be feasible/decidable.

### Semantic gap

A term has multiple incompatible meanings.

### Governance gap

A policy/authority rule is undefined.

### Architecture gap

An architectural conclusion does not follow from the theory.

### Empirical gap

A claim has not been experimentally demonstrated.

